From: OpenIPC
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt7601sta: keep the adapter in CAM power mode

The power saving this driver is built with is not usable here: an associated
link that MlmeCheckPsmChange() puts into PWR_SAVE stops passing traffic, and
the idle path switches the radio off outright (0003). Pin WindowsPowerMode to
CAM after the profile is read, so that a PSMode line in the .dat -- or anything
else that sets it -- cannot put the link to sleep.

--- a/common/cmm_profile.c
+++ b/common/cmm_profile.c
@@ -4022,6 +4022,12 @@
 									pAd->StaCfg.WindowsPowerMode = Ndis802_11PowerModeCAM;
 								pAd->StaCfg.WindowsBatteryPowerMode = Ndis802_11PowerModeCAM;
 							}
+							/* CAM is not optional on this chip: an associated link that is
+							 * put into PWR_SAVE wakes up deaf, and the idle path would switch
+							 * the radio off outright. Whatever the profile asked for, stay
+							 * awake. */
+							RTMP_SET_PSM_BIT(pAd, PWR_ACTIVE);
+							pAd->StaCfg.WindowsPowerMode = Ndis802_11PowerModeCAM;
 							DBGPRINT(RT_DEBUG_TRACE, ("PSMode=%ld\n", pAd->StaCfg.WindowsPowerMode));
 						}
 					}
